From 400728a384a3f90456ff02940eb8237a49a005d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:37:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] aurora: a gxcore draw's constants as immediate data, read
 from storage

The render worker set two bind groups for nearly every draw: group 1,
the vertex block's three dynamic-offset parts, and group 2, the pixel
constants. On a slow core each set cost about 330 ns of encoding and
submitting (Dawn's front end and the D3D12 back end), and with Smooth
Motion every pass is encoded again for each in-between frame: at
Forest Haven, 120 Hz on two E-cores, 5,300 vertex-block and 1,900
pixel-constant sets a game frame, 2 of the render worker's 5 ms. 0142's
three parts had made each vertex-block set dearer (1.3 ms a game frame
there).

Where the device has immediate data and WGSL's immediate address
space, the generated modules read their constants from storage:
gxcore's immediate_constants_wgsl rewrites vsc., vsm., vsl. and psc.
reads into loads at rows of the frame's constant buffer (or the
in-between frames', kConstantsInBetween), and a draw's 16 bytes of
immediate data (DrawConstants) say where its vertex block, matrix
memory, lights and pixel constants are. Group 1 is the two constant
buffers, bound once a pass; the TEV path's group 2 is an empty group.
A draw sets its immediate data when its rows change, and no group is
set again for a pipeline change (each group's object fixes its
layout). The device asks for four storage buffers a stage and the
adapter's storage binding size; DOL_AURORA_IMMEDIATE_CONSTANTS=0, or a
device without immediate data, keeps the dynamic-offset bindings.

Smooth Motion dumps at seven places identical, real and in-between
frames. Encoding and submitting a game frame (Smooth Motion at 120,
two E-cores): Forest Haven 5.2 -> 3.6 ms, Hyrule Castle's room 3.3 ->
2.5, Outset 2.6 -> 2.1, Dragon Roost 3.9 -> 3.3.

Also: DOL_AURORA_ENCODE_STATS=1 logs what the render worker hands Dawn
a game frame ([encode-stats]: passes, draws, binds, pipelines, vertex
buffers, immediates, encode and submit ms), and DOL_AURORA_GPU_PROF's
lines count the staging copy commands (copies=).
